\par\par \b \uc2 Uncertainty Over Potential \uc2 Samsung\uc2 , \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2  Capex Likely Weighing on Shares -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 167 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2026\par 07:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0513 GMT - Uncertainty over \uc2 Samsung Electronics\uc2 ' and \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2 's potential capital-expenditure is likely pressuring their share prices, says \uc2 Morningstar\uc2 's Jing Jie Yu in commentary. The two companies could be planning to spend around a combined 2 quadrillion won over the next decade, nearly double \uc2 Morningstar\uc2 's capex estimates. This could include \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2 's plans to invest in \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  data centers, with its Yongin fab cluster commitments already expected at 600 trillion won, he notes. Should \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2 's AI data center commitment and its potential capex plans be separate, the analyst flags material risk of oversupply for memory producers, given that demand tends to taper off during the tail years of capex cycles. \uc2 Samsung\uc2  shares fall 6.5% to 317,000 won, while \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2  shares drop 4.7% to 2,548,000 won. (megan.cheah@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 29, 2026 01:13 ET (05:13 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260629em6t000cg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
